insert into public.admin_fields (entity, record_id, field, value) values ('Lesson', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b10', 'internal_notes', 'Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3f1ca793c2c58172a548c1e889b65991 — rebuilt Oct 12 2026 from Build Otherwise copy (Oct 6)

Former approval_note (removed because the app shows this field on the card): Replacement approved by Ashley Zeck, 2026-10-14 (chat decision: go live now). Source: Lesson_O1-O5_only.csv.') on conflict (entity, record_id, field) do update set value = excluded.value;
insert into public.lesson ("alias", "approval_note", "approval_state", "approved_source", "approved_version", "boundary", "carry_forward", "code", "decision_options", "description", "duration_min", "has_decision", "module_order", "order", "purpose", "readings_note", "reflect_prompts", "routes", "show", "status", "teach", "title", "try_prompts", "type", "what_comes_out", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('3', null, 'pending_approval', 'Entrepalooza Pilot 1 — Module Breakdown (Oct 5, 2026) · adopted Pilot 1 scope', 'Pilot 1 adopted card · lessons database copy Oct 6, 2026', 'Keep participant choice, the right to pass, and facilitator boundaries intact. Skipped or blank answers are saved as “no response,” never as a decision.', '["O.6"]'::jsonb, 'M1-L1', '[]'::jsonb, 'Notice a possible interest, question, frustration, or unfamiliar opportunity. Separate what caught attention from the meaning you assign it; choose whether to investigate further.', 10, false, 1, 1, 'Explore where possible interests come from and identify a question worth investigating.', null, '[]'::jsonb, '["Use something I noticed","Bring a Life Map thread","Explore something unfamiliar","Nothing draws me in yet","Pass"]'::jsonb, '', 'draft', 'Interests are not always discovered by looking inward. They can develop through exposure, practice, conversation, necessity, and chance. You might notice a problem you want solved, a subject you keep returning to, or an unfamiliar activity you would like to experience. You may also have no clear candidate yet.

Attention is not the same as enjoyment or commitment. Repeatedly thinking about something can reflect responsibility or worry as well as curiosity. What matters is investigating *why* it has your attention, rather than declaring it your passion.

Choose something from your Life Map, an ordinary observation, or an unfamiliar topic you want to learn about. If nothing comes to mind, notice one activity or question you encounter during the coming week. This is an invitation to explore, not a test of self-knowledge.', 'Notice what draws your attention', '["What is one activity, subject, question, or problem you might want to understand better?","What would you need to encounter, ask, or try to find out whether it interests you?"]'::jsonb, 'activity', 'A participant-selected observation, possible question, or honest uncertainty to bring into Module 2.', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b12', '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-19T01:13:54.948000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "alias" = excluded."alias", "approval_note" = excluded."approval_note", "approval_state" = excluded."approval_state", "approved_source" = excluded."approved_source", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "boundary" = excluded."boundary", "carry_forward" = excluded."carry_forward", "code" = excluded."code", "decision_options" = excluded."decision_options", "description" = excluded."description", "duration_min" = excluded."duration_min", "has_decision" = excluded."has_decision", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "order" = excluded."order", "purpose" = excluded."purpose", "readings_note" = excluded."readings_note", "reflect_prompts" = excluded."reflect_prompts", "routes" = excluded."routes", "show" = excluded."show", "status" = excluded."status", "teach" = excluded."teach", "title" = excluded."title", "try_prompts" = excluded."try_prompts", "type" = excluded."type", "what_comes_out" = excluded."what_comes_out", "created_date" = excluded."created_date", "updated_date" = excluded."updated_date";
insert into public.admin_fields (entity, record_id, field, value) values ('Lesson', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b12', 'internal_notes', 'Garden flow approved for Base44 handoff only; the no-Decide exception (skipping the shared Next Decision step) is still open. Do not treat skipped responses as decisions.

BUILD SPEC (moved out of participant teach text, Oct 14 2026):
#### 1. Choose how to enter

**What would you like to work with today?**

- Something that caught my attention
- A thread from my Life Map
- The garden example
- I''m not sure yet (goes to the garden example)
Routing: "Something that caught my attention" and "A thread from my Life Map" go straight to step 3, with the garden example offered as an optional look first. "The garden example" and "I''m not sure yet" go to step 2.
Every step has a visible **Skip** that moves to the next step without an answer.
Rights reminder under the step 1 question (Claude''s suggested wording, not Ashley''s): "You can use the example, skip any step, or pass without explaining."

#### 2. Explore the garden example

> Someone keeps noticing community gardens. They don''t yet know whether it''s the gardening, food, people, or being outside that interests them.
>

Tap a category for each statement: **"The example tells us this"** or **"Someone added this conclusion."**

| Statement | Feedback after choosing |
| --- | --- |
| They keep noticing community gardens. | That''s in the example. It''s a starting point, not a commitment. |
| Gardening is their passion. | That adds a conclusion. We don''t know which part interests them yet. |
| They aren''t sure what draws them in. | The example tells us they''re unsure. An unknown is useful information too. |
| They should start a gardening business. | That jumps from noticing to a destination they haven''t chosen. |

No score or right/wrong marks. Just an explanation and a chance to look again.

#### 3. Make it useful

Heading by entry path. Own thread: **What caught your attention, and what don''t you know yet?** Example: **What might be drawing them in, and what might they want to find out?**
Using your own thread: jot down a few words for each part.
Using the example, two quick picks:

- What might be drawing them in? **the gardening · the food · the people · being outside** (more than one allowed) or **still unclear** (choosing it clears the others)
- What might they want to find out? **which part matters most · what it would be like to try · how it might fit into their week**
Either pick, or both, can be skipped.

#### 4. Leave with a possibility

**What might help you learn a little more?**

- Look again
- Find out about one part
- Ask a question
- Nothing for now
After step 4, whatever they chose (or if they skipped), everyone sees: "You can look again, learn a little more, ask a question, or leave it for now."
**The takeaway:** "Noticing gives you somewhere to begin. It doesn''t tell you who you are or what you have to do next."
Build note: no Next Decision field in this lesson. Skips and blank answers are saved as "no response," never as Continue Looking or any other label.

