Former boundary/source text: Source draft: `05-module-0-facilitator-guide.md` (30–42 min Code + feedback practice) and `07-modules-0-1-participant-packet.md` (**P0.2**). This is working curriculum content and remains in **Draft** until rehearsed. Keep participant choice, the right to pass, and facilitator boundaries intact.
Source pages (Ashley Zeck workspace): [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/b7a4e722bdf582f2b31781b8928c479e?pvs=21) · [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/a484e722bdf58371b7a381c08ebacb96?pvs=21)') on conflict (entity, record_id, field) do update set value = excluded.value;
insert into public.lesson ("alias", "approval_note", "approval_state", "approved_source", "approved_version", "boundary", "carry_forward", "code", "decision_options", "description", "duration_min", "has_decision", "module_order", "order", "purpose", "readings_note", "reflect_prompts", "routes", "show", "status", "teach", "title", "try_prompts", "type", "what_comes_out", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('Life Map', null, 'pending_approval', 'Entrepalooza Pilot 1 — Module Breakdown (Oct 5, 2026) · adopted Pilot 1 scope', 'Pilot 1 adopted card · lessons database copy Oct 6, 2026', null, '[]'::jsonb, 'O.6', '[]'::jsonb, 'Put your real week on one page before planning anything.', 30, false, 0, 6, 'Notice what already occupies your time, attention, energy, movement, and relationships before deciding what might be worth exploring.', null, '["Which line surprised you?","What''s still missing?"]'::jsonb, '["Add lines","Link a journal entry","Observe","Come back later","Pass","Pause or stop"]'::jsonb, '“Places: the community kitchen, two bus rides away. The library, a ten-minute walk.”  
“Energy: steadier after making something. Drained after a day of meetings.”  
No conclusions yet. Just what’s true.', 'draft', 'This exercise starts with what your life actually looks like right now, not with a passion, a business idea, or a life purpose.

Ordinary places and activities often get left out when someone is asked to “tell me about yourself.” The map is a way to notice them. You’ll put the places you regularly go on one page — grocery, library, work, school, transit, relatives, parks, services, or wherever you actually go — and add the activities that don’t have a clear physical place (online research, phone calls, caregiving at home, job searching from a library or living room). Mark energy, curiosity, and barriers with whatever symbols you choose.

What is missing can matter as much as what is present. A place or activity may be absent because you don’t currently care about it, or because you can’t currently reach it (transit, money, schedule, distance, childcare). Both are information. Barriers are practical constraints, not mindset problems.

The map is a snapshot of this moment. It can change. Empty sections are honest. Nothing is scored. You can keep the whole map private, share only one section, or stop and return later. It is evidence of where your life is right now. It does not tell you who you are or what you must do next.', 'Map your life right now', '[]'::jsonb, 'tool', 'A map you can add to, change, download, and keep private, with journal entries linked wherever you choose. Nothing here is scored.', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b11', '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "alias" = excluded."alias", "approval_note" = excluded."approval_note", "approval_state" = excluded."approval_state", "approved_source" = excluded."approved_source", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "boundary" = excluded."boundary", "carry_forward" = excluded."carry_forward", "code" = excluded."code", "decision_options" = excluded."decision_options", "description" = excluded."description", "duration_min" = excluded."duration_min", "has_decision" = excluded."has_decision", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "order" = excluded."order", "purpose" = excluded."purpose", "readings_note" = excluded."readings_note", "reflect_prompts" = excluded."reflect_prompts", "routes" = excluded."routes", "show" = excluded."show", "status" = excluded."status", "teach" = excluded."teach", "title" = excluded."title", "try_prompts" = excluded."try_prompts", "type" = excluded."type", "what_comes_out" = excluded."what_comes_out", "created_date" = excluded."created_date", "updated_date" = excluded."updated_date";
insert into public.admin_fields (entity, record_id, field, value) values ('Lesson', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b11', 'internal_notes', 'Previous source/boundary note (staff only): Empty sections are honest too. Nothing here has to be finished, and nothing is scored.

Getting Started rewrite applied from attached draft (Oct 9, 2026). Staff tasks — do not show participants:

Interactive idea (not implemented): On the map, let people tap quick-add chips for each area (e.g. Barriers: Cost · Transport · Childcare · Schedule · Access · Credentials) before typing anything.
Privacy/storage claims in the supplied draft require verification against the app implementation before launch; O.2 keeps cautious participant wording until confirmed.
Shared UI changes are not implemented by lesson-record edits:


### Participation choices (replaces [PC])

Every way of taking part counts the same, and you can switch anytime. Passing never needs a reason.

### Next decision intro (replaces [ND])

Pick the one that fits today. "I don''t know yet" is fine, and you can change it later.

### Next decision buttons (replaces [NDL])

Keep | Change | Test again | Pause | Stop | Another direction | Keep looking

### Privacy line (replaces [SV], [EV], and [DK])

Once per page, under "Your turn":

> 🔒 Your answers stay in this browser and your private journal. Nothing is sent to Entrepalooza unless you choose to share it or use the feedback button.

Under each answer box, next to the Dictate button (short version):

> Private: stays in this browser.

### Feedback prompt (replaces [FB])

Something unclear on this page? Tell us. [Send feedback]
(What you send here does go to the Entrepalooza team.)

### Site footer (replaces [FOOTER])

Pilot 1 covers Getting Started and Modules 1–5. What you type stays in this browser unless you choose to share it.
This is a learning workbook, not therapy or treatment.
Questions or concerns: [ASHLEY: add the confirmed support and concern contacts here before launch]

### Removed everywhere

- The "Approved source: Entrepalooza Pilot 1 — Module Breakdown…" line ([SRC])
- All "Source and boundaries" sections and their author notes
- All [FILL] placeholders
- The heading "SHOW — A NEUTRAL EXAMPLE, NEVER A PARTICIPANT STORY" (now "Example")

FACILITATOR NOTE (moved out of participant text):
### Facilitator note

Do not interpret the participant''s map for them.
Avoid:

> "Your map shows that you''re isolated."
>

Use:

> "What do you notice?"
>

Avoid:

> "Clearly you''re passionate about cars."
>

Use:

> "You marked that in three different places. Does that mean anything to you?"
>

The research treats the map and the participant''s explanation together. The visual alone is not supposed to speak for the person who made it.
And because participants choose what to include, visual methods can give them greater control over what becomes part of the conversation.') on conflict (entity, record_id, field) do update set value = excluded.value;
insert into public.lesson ("alias", "approval_note", "approval_state", "approved_source", "approved_version", "boundary", "carry_forward", "code", "decision_options", "description", "duration_min", "has_decision", "module_order", "order", "purpose", "readings_note", "reflect_prompts", "routes", "show", "status", "teach", "title", "try_prompts", "type", "what_comes_out", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('6', null, 'pending_approval', 'Entrepalooza Pilot 1 — Module Breakdown (Oct 5, 2026) · adopted Pilot 1 scope', 'Pilot 1 adopted card · lessons database copy Oct 6, 2026', 'Source draft: `06-module-1-facilitator-guide.md`. This is working curriculum content and remains in **Draft** until rehearsed. Keep participant choice, the right to pass, and facilitator boundaries intact.
Source pages (Ashley Zeck workspace): [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/b7a4e722bdf582f2b31781b8928c479e?pvs=21) · [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/a484e722bdf58371b7a381c08ebacb96?pvs=21)', '["M2-L1"]'::jsonb, 'M2-L2', '[]'::jsonb, 'Act on one possibility, or observe if participation is not possible, and gather a few useful observations without a long questionnaire.', 10, false, 2, 2, 'Experience one manageable activity or observe it, then notice what actually happened.', null, '["","What kind of encounter did you actually have: reading, watching, a conversation, a visit, doing an activity yourself, or a combination? If you did not have an opportunity, record that.","At what point did your attention change? Was there a particular part you wanted to understand better?","How did the people, setting, instructions, or available support affect the experience? What remains uncertain?"]'::jsonb, '["I tried something","I observed or spoke with someone","I couldn''t access an opportunity yet","Pass"]'::jsonb, '', 'draft', '## Learn by encountering something

The smallest useful experiment may be watching someone work, asking a question, visiting a place, or trying a beginner activity. It doesn''t have to become a project or business.

If you saved a plan on the last step, bring it into this one and start there. That plan is what you are noticing.

If you have an activity from the previous lesson, try it when you have a realistic opportunity. You can also switch to a different possibility. Don''t risk your safety, spend money you can''t spare, or neglect important responsibilities to finish a workbook step.

## What did you actually learn?

Notice what happened before deciding what it says about you. Enjoying a demonstration doesn''t necessarily mean you''d like the daily work. Difficulty on a first attempt doesn''t prove you lack ability. Access, instructions, support, and time all affect what you can experience.

If you couldn''t try anything, that matters too: what prevented access, and would another route be more realistic? You can return to this lesson after an experience.

## Notice the parts and the kind of encounter

Reading, watching, talking with someone, visiting, and doing an activity yourself provide different kinds of information. Name what you actually encountered. Watching an enjoyable demonstration does not establish how doing the activity would feel.

Notice changes within the experience: where your attention increased or faded, which parts raised questions, and how the people, setting, instructions, or support shaped what happened. Write privately, talk it through, or combine both. Give your answers honest, thoughtful attention without inventing a result.', 'Give It a Try—and Notice', '["What caught your attention?","What did you actually do or observe?","What surprised, frustrated, or interested you?","What helped or made participation difficult?","What did it take in time, money, energy, or support?","","","","",""]'::jsonb, 'reflection', 'Keep a brief record of what happened, or a question to investigate when an opportunity becomes available.', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b15', '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-24T07:55:29.611000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "alias" = excluded."alias", "approval_note" = excluded."approval_note", "approval_state" = excluded."approval_state", "approved_source" = excluded."approved_source", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "boundary" = excluded."boundary", "carry_forward" = excluded."carry_forward", "code" = excluded."code", "decision_options" = excluded."decision_options", "description" = excluded."description", "duration_min" = excluded."duration_min", "has_decision" = excluded."has_decision", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "order" = excluded."order", "purpose" = excluded."purpose", "readings_note" = excluded."readings_note", "reflect_prompts" = excluded."reflect_prompts", "routes" = excluded."routes", "show" = excluded."show", "status" = excluded."status", "teach" = excluded."teach", "title" = excluded."title", "try_prompts" = excluded."try_prompts", "type" = excluded."type", "what_comes_out" = excluded."what_comes_out", "created_date" = excluded."created_date", "updated_date" = excluded."updated_date";
insert into public.lesson ("alias", "approval_note", "approval_state", "approved_source", "approved_version", "boundary", "carry_forward", "code", "decision_options", "description", "duration_min", "has_decision", "module_order", "order", "purpose", "readings_note", "reflect_prompts", "routes", "show", "status", "teach", "title", "try_prompts", "type", "what_comes_out", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('1', null, 'pending_approval', 'Breakdown — Pilot 1 (3f1ca793c2c5818ea667d1383885ea7a) · Lessons — Modules 0, 4–8 (3f1ca793c2c581108a93fc2df2c9f49e)', 'Build Otherwise copy of Lessons database, Oct 6, 2026 (copy of live Ashley Zeck workspace source; not rehearsed)', 'Don’t collect addiction, legal, or diagnostic histories to prove eligibility. Keep participation, evaluation, recording, story use, and follow-up as separate choices.', '[]'::jsonb, 'O.2', '[]'::jsonb, 'Review who can see records, how records can be corrected, how to raise a concern, and the right to pass without explanation. Keep participation, evaluation, recording, publicity/story use, and follow-up as separate choices. Do not collect addiction, legal, or diagnostic histories to prove eligibility.', 10, false, 0, 2, 'Know your rights here, what stays private, and how to fix or raise something.', null, '["What''s clearer about privacy now? What do you still want to ask?"]'::jsonb, '["Say it","Write it","Watch","Pass"]'::jsonb, '**Example:** Someone is asked whether a session can be recorded. They answer: “Yes to taking part. No to recording. Not now on follow-up.” Each answer stands on its own.', 'draft', 'You decide what you share. Passing on a personal question never needs an explanation.

Taking part, evaluation, recording, using your story, and follow-up are separate choices. Saying yes to one does not mean yes to the others. Each one gets its own Yes, No, or Not now.

What you write in the workbook stays in your account. Other participants can’t see it. You can ask who can see what’s stored, ask for a correction, or download or delete what you’ve written. You will never be asked for medical, legal, or personal history to take part.', 'Your rights and privacy', '["One right you plan to use here (for example, passing without explaining).","One choice you''d want kept separate: evaluation, recording, your story, or follow-up."]'::jsonb, 'orientation', 'A short record or observation. Private and pass routes count.', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b0d', '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-23T02:12:02.906000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "alias" = excluded."alias", "approval_note" = excluded."approval_note", "approval_state" = excluded."approval_state", "approved_source" = excluded."approved_source", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "boundary" = excluded."boundary", "carry_forward" = excluded."carry_forward", "code" = excluded."code", "decision_options" = excluded."decision_options", "description" = excluded."description", "duration_min" = excluded."duration_min", "has_decision" = excluded."has_decision", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "order" = excluded."order", "purpose" = excluded."purpose", "readings_note" = excluded."readings_note", "reflect_prompts" = excluded."reflect_prompts", "routes" = excluded."routes", "show" = excluded."show", "status" = excluded."status", "teach" = excluded."teach", "title" = excluded."title", "try_prompts" = excluded."try_prompts", "type" = excluded."type", "what_comes_out" = excluded."what_comes_out", "created_date" = excluded."created_date", "updated_date" = excluded."updated_date";
insert into public.admin_fields (entity, record_id, field, value) values ('Lesson', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b0d', 'internal_notes', 'RETIRED from the app Oct 23, 2026 (Ashley approved option B): rights and privacy folded into O.1. Hidden by src/lib/gettingStartedContent.js (RETIRED_GS_CODES). Record kept for history and for the /preview learning pack.

Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3f1ca793c2c58138bdace07addce0cd3 — rebuilt Oct 12 2026 from Build Otherwise copy (Oct 6)

Ops notes (moved from participant text, not yet confirmed): If any of those routes are still [FILL] on P0.1 or the privacy notice, state that the arrangement is not yet confirmed rather than improvising a contact. | **WATCH — ops still [FILL]:** Privacy notice (custodian, access, storage, retention/deletion, correction), complaint route and alternative-to-facilitator contact, and separate consent documents remain OPEN until staff confirm. Do not fabricate contact numbers or policies. If a required arrangement is absent, defer the affected delivery rather than asking participants to accept an unknown policy.

Former approval_note (removed because the app shows this field on the card): Replacement approved by Ashley Zeck, 2026-10-14 (chat decision: go live now). Source: Lesson_O1-O5_only.csv.

Former boundary/source text: Source draft: `05-module-0-facilitator-guide.md` (15–25 min rights/privacy/consent; consent handling) and `07-modules-0-1-participant-packet.md` (P0.1 privacy lines; P0.4 separate-permission language). Related ops packet mention on this lesson’s Resource Links: Module 0 Operational Packet. This is working curriculum content and remains in **Draft** until rehearsed.
Source pages (Ashley Zeck workspace): [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/b7a4e722bdf582f2b31781b8928c479e?pvs=21) · [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/a484e722bdf58371b7a381c08ebacb96?pvs=21) · [‣](https://app.notion.com/p/3e64e722bdf581be931bd1b30f4737ec?pvs=21)') on conflict (entity, record_id, field) do update set value = excluded.value;
insert into public.lesson ("alias", "approval_note", "approval_state", "approved_source", "approved_version", "boundary", "carry_forward", "code", "decision_options", "description", "duration_min", "has_decision", "module_order", "order", "purpose", "readings_note", "reflect_prompts", "routes", "show", "status", "teach", "title", "try_prompts", "type", "what_comes_out", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('2.3', null, 'pending_approval', 'Breakdown — Pilot 1 (3f1ca793c2c5818ea667d1383885ea7a) · Lessons — Modules 0, 4–8 (3f1ca793c2c581108a93fc2df2c9f49e)', 'Build Otherwise copy of Lessons database, Oct 6, 2026 (copy of live Ashley Zeck workspace source; not rehearsed)', 'This plan is not a consent form. Consent choices are a separate record completed later.', '[]'::jsonb, 'O.4', '[]'::jsonb, 'Optional, private “What makes it work for you” lines (formerly the Participation and Support Plan): how you''d like to take part, what makes it harder to show up, and support you''d want (or none). No diagnoses or histories. Never sent.', 3, false, 0, 4, 'Optional. A few lines so taking part fits your life.', null, '[]'::jsonb, '["Say it","Write it","Watch","Pass"]'::jsonb, '**Example:** “Phone only, limited data. I work Saturdays. No extra support for now.”', 'draft', 'This step is optional. Fill it in now, later, or not at all. It doesn’t hold anything up.

Fill in what’s useful. Leave the rest blank. “None” and “I don’t know yet” are complete answers.

This stays private in your workbook. If you want Ashley to know something, email Start@buildotherwise.org.', 'What makes it work for you', '["","","How you’d like to take part (for example: writing, voice, mostly reading first)","Anything that makes it harder to show up (time, phone or data, access, other)","Support you’d want, or “none for now”"]'::jsonb, 'orientation', null, '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b0f', '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-23T02:59:27.403000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "alias" = excluded."alias", "approval_note" = excluded."approval_note", "approval_state" = excluded."approval_state", "approved_source" = excluded."approved_source", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "boundary" = excluded."boundary", "carry_forward" = excluded."carry_forward", "code" = excluded."code", "decision_options" = excluded."decision_options", "description" = excluded."description", "duration_min" = excluded."duration_min", "has_decision" = excluded."has_decision", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "order" = excluded."order", "purpose" = excluded."purpose", "readings_note" = excluded."readings_note", "reflect_prompts" = excluded."reflect_prompts", "routes" = excluded."routes", "show" = excluded."show", "status" = excluded."status", "teach" = excluded."teach", "title" = excluded."title", "try_prompts" = excluded."try_prompts", "type" = excluded."type", "what_comes_out" = excluded."what_comes_out", "created_date" = excluded."created_date", "updated_date" = excluded."updated_date";
insert into public.admin_fields (entity, record_id, field, value) values ('Lesson', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b0f', 'internal_notes', 'Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3f1ca793c2c581888a18dc9aaf034981 — rebuilt Oct 12 2026 from Build Otherwise copy (Oct 6)

Ops notes (moved from participant text, not yet confirmed): This plan is not a consent form — consent choices are a separate record completed later. **WATCH — ops still [FILL]:** support and concern contacts must match the confirmed P0.1 routes. Do not invent contacts. Remains **Draft** until rehearsed.

Former approval_note (removed because the app shows this field on the card): Replacement approved by Ashley Zeck, 2026-10-14 (chat decision: go live now). Source: Lesson_O1-O5_only.csv.') on conflict (entity, record_id, field) do update set value = excluded.value;
insert into public.lesson ("alias", "approval_note", "approval_state", "approved_source", "approved_version", "boundary", "carry_forward", "code", "decision_options", "description", "duration_min", "has_decision", "module_order", "order", "purpose", "readings_note", "reflect_prompts", "routes", "show", "status", "teach", "title", "try_prompts", "type", "what_comes_out", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('4', null, 'pending_approval', 'Entrepalooza Pilot 1 — Module Breakdown (Oct 5, 2026) · adopted Pilot 1 scope', 'Pilot 1 adopted card · lessons database copy Oct 6, 2026', 'Keep participant choice, the right to pass, and facilitator boundaries intact. No scoring and no labeling anyone ‘obsessive.’', '[]'::jsonb, 'M1-L2', '[]'::jsonb, 'Notice that time, intensity, or repeated attention is not yet a passion or a commitment.', 15, false, 1, 2, 'Notice that time, intensity, or repeated attention is not yet a passion or a commitment.', null, '["What is one question about choice, pressure, or flexibility that this reading raises for you?"]'::jsonb, '["Read the caution","Consider an activity I know","Pass"]'::jsonb, '', 'draft', 'Repeated attention is not a passion. You might think about something often because you are curious, because you are worried, or because someone needs you to. Spending a lot of time on it does not, by itself, tell you that it fits the rest of your life or that you should continue.

You do not need to judge how intense an interest is in this module. A question, or an honest unknown, is enough. Module 5, Tuning Your Instrument, is where you listen to how an activity is going, including intensity, choice, and pressure, after you have had a chance to try something.

If an activity already matters to you, you can notice whether you still have a choice about it. You do not have to decide that now.', 'Attention is not a passion', '[]'::jsonb, 'reading', 'A question to revisit, if useful.', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b13', '2026-10-16T02:30:05.273000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-20T03:21:03.412000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "alias" = excluded."alias", "approval_note" = excluded."approval_note", "approval_state" = excluded."approval_state", "approved_source" = excluded."approved_source", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "boundary" = excluded."boundary", "carry_forward" = excluded."carry_forward", "code" = excluded."code", "decision_options" = excluded."decision_options", "description" = excluded."description", "duration_min" = excluded."duration_min", "has_decision" = excluded."has_decision", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "order" = excluded."order", "purpose" = excluded."purpose", "readings_note" = excluded."readings_note", "reflect_prompts" = excluded."reflect_prompts", "routes" = excluded."routes", "show" = excluded."show", "status" = excluded."status", "teach" = excluded."teach", "title" = excluded."title", "try_prompts" = excluded."try_prompts", "type" = excluded."type", "what_comes_out" = excluded."what_comes_out", "created_date" = excluded."created_date", "updated_date" = excluded."updated_date";
insert into public.admin_fields (entity, record_id, field, value) values ('Lesson', '6ad18c2d5550b97a5e042b13', 'internal_notes', '19 Oct 2026. The Dualistic Model of Passion was moved to Module 5 (M5-L1 and its reading). This lesson keeps a caution: attention, time, and intensity are not a passion and not a commitment. Do not teach harmonious or obsessive passion here. 20 Oct 2026. The open tribe thread on this step asks what else attention can be. It does not ask when love becomes demanding. Module 5 is titled Tuning Your Instrument.') on conflict (entity, record_id, field) do update set value = excluded.value;
