insert into public.lesson_review_package ("instructional_purpose", "lesson_code", "lesson_id", "reviewer_notes", "research_rationale", "proposed_draft_text", "decision_note", "decided_date", "source_label", "facilitator_boundaries", "source_url", "module_title", "lesson_title", "current_card_note", "review_scope", "review_status", "approval_decision", "approved_version", "research_limitations", "internal_notes", "module_order", "participation_alternatives", "approver", "changes_requested", "source_date", "proposed_draft_label", "id", "created_date", "updated_date") values ('Help participants test internal assumptions against ethical, accessible information from the outside world. Everyone learns a shared evidence-checking method and then chooses a pathway, problem/opportunity, or continued-exploration branch.
Module 4 begins with a question—not a pitch. It does not require a business idea, direct interview, customer, market, unmet need, offer, or progression to Module 5.', 'M6-L4', '6acfad71713aa2815e104ecc', 'Tribe thread: Peer feedback lab on evidence labels (observation vs assumption). Honest peer screening > cheerleading. No extracting free research from vulnerable people.

Proposed prompts inside the draft text are recommendations for review, not approved participant instructions.', 'Research: See sibling Research Brief — All Modules under this Live Curriculum parent. Key cites (analogous): Sarasvathy 2001 effectuation · Leatherbee & Katila 2020 · Kolb experiential learning. Equal branches; no validate/demand claims.', 'Shared fit review
Compare external evidence with:
- Interest and meaning
- Helpful operating conditions
- Required time, energy, interaction, resources, and uncertainty
- Access and practical barriers
- Cost to health, relationships, responsibilities, rest, and support
- Whether engagement remains chosen, flexible, and sustainable

Problem/opportunity fit
Only for participants on the problem/opportunity branch. Retain Problem Fit × Builder Fit as a non-scored conversation:
- Is the problem supported by evidence?
- Does the participant want to keep investigating it?
- Do the demands and conditions fit—or could they be made workable?
- What would make the answer change?
A strong external opportunity with poor participant fit is not automatically the right direction. Pathway and continued-exploration participants skip this box and use the shared fit review above.

What comes out
A fit observation, known barrier or support, and revision condition.

Choose one:
- Continue
- Redefine
- Research
- Park
- Stop
- Another Direction
- Continue Looking

Branch destinations

Problem/opportunity destination
Participants may move into an ethical response or offer test. Question: “Will this small response teach me something useful about the problem and the people affected?”

Pathway destination
Participants may test one real pathway step, such as a class sample, beginner task, work sample, informational conversation, job shadow, bounded volunteer role, program visit, or review of actual requirements and costs. Question: “Does this path still fit after I experience one real part of it?”

Continued-exploration destination
Participants may gather more information, compare options, repeat exposure, pause, or return later. They are not required to advance into a test.', '', null, 'Notion — Entrepalooza Curriculum & Evidence Lab · Module 4 working draft · Copy of Ashley Zeck workspace original · Oct 6, 2026 · edits here do not sync. Cross-links may still point to Ashley-workspace originals until rewritten.', '- Do not steer participants toward business ownership.
- Do not treat all friction as an opportunity to monetize.
- Keep structural and practical barriers visible.
- Do not require cold outreach, travel, spending, public disclosure, or direct interviews.
- Do not describe one example as validation.
- Ask whose perspective is missing and who may bear cost.
- Preserve participant choice to park, stop, redirect, or continue looking.

- Do not ask vulnerable people for trauma stories, unpaid emotional labor, or free consulting.
- Do not present a learning conversation as formal research, treatment, employment, partnership, or a promised solution.
- Ask permission before taking notes, quoting, recording, or sharing information.
- Do not collect identifying or sensitive information without an approved process.
- Accept no, nonresponse, cancellation, and limited access as real outcomes.
- Use public, neutral, or simulated routes when direct contact is inappropriate or inaccessible.
- Do not treat one conversation as proof of demand, prevalence, or validation.
- Do not assume every observed problem should become a business opportunity.', 'https://www.notion.so/3f1ca793c2c5819c948ff3bbcc283ddb', 'Check Reality Outside Yourself', 'Check fit and choose your next discovery decision', 'Existing card retained unchanged, as structure. Teaching on this card is not approved for participant delivery.', 'Outside questions, evidence gathering, relevant branches, and personal fit versus actual availability.', 'pending_evaluator_and_clinical_review', '', '', 'Research and theory are used as design lenses, not as proof that Entrepalooza works. Related research does not prove that Entrepalooza works.', '', 6, 'Pass, respond in private, observe, pause, stop, or choose another direction.
A missing worksheet is not a failed module.
Every decision fits one of these labels: Keep, Change, Test Again, Pause/Park, Stop, Another Direction, Continue Looking. "Still don''t know" lives under Continue Looking.', '', 'Status: Working replacement draft for review and rehearsal. The current Module 4 lesson pages remain unchanged until this draft is approved. This draft provides a shared evidence foundation followed by pathway, problem/opportunity, and continued-exploration branches.', 'Oct 6, 2026', 'Review candidate — working replacement draft. Not approved teaching, and not part of the participant workbook.', '6ac8a3de20a10ee24ca3e1df', '2026-10-09T08:20:46.097000'::timestamptz, '2026-10-14T16:33:51.221000'::timestamptz) on conflict (id) do update set "instructional_purpose" = excluded."instructional_purpose", "lesson_code" = excluded."lesson_code", "lesson_id" = excluded."lesson_id", "reviewer_notes" = excluded."reviewer_notes", "research_rationale" = excluded."research_rationale", "proposed_draft_text" = excluded."proposed_draft_text", "decision_note" = excluded."decision_note", "decided_date" = excluded."decided_date", "source_label" = excluded."source_label", "facilitator_boundaries" = excluded."facilitator_boundaries", "source_url" = excluded."source_url", "module_title" = excluded."module_title", "lesson_title" = excluded."lesson_title", "current_card_note" = excluded."current_card_note", "review_scope" = excluded."review_scope", "review_status" = excluded."review_status", "approval_decision" = excluded."approval_decision", "approved_version" = excluded."approved_version", "research_limitations" = excluded."research_limitations", "internal_notes" = excluded."internal_notes", "module_order" = excluded."module_order", "participation_alternatives" = excluded."participation_alternatives", "approver" = excluded."approver", "changes_requested" = excluded."changes_requested", "source_date" = excluded."source_date", "proposed_draft_label" = excluded."proposed_draft_label", "created_date" = excluded."create