Proposed prompts inside the draft text are recommendations for review, not approved participant instructions.', 'Research: See sibling Research Guide — Modules 6–8 + Tribe under this Live Curriculum parent. Key cites: Kaiser et al. 2022 · Sarasvathy affordable loss · Fernandes et al. 2014. Proposed — not adopted until Ashley approves.

Analogous support: Kaiser et al. 2022 financial-education RCT meta; Miller et al. record-keeping; Sarasvathy affordable loss. Counters: Fernandes et al. 2014 knowledge–behavior gap (weaker in low-income samples). Design analogy only — not an Entrepalooza outcome claim.', 'Why this matters
Money is evidence connected to experience—not theater for a business that barely exists.

Neutral demonstration
$0 received, scrap-paper cost, owned pen/paper, forgotten time to count later. Still a complete honest map.

Try—or pass
List spend / receive / owned / borrowed / forgotten. Mark revenue vs kept. Note what stays private. Fictional, private, or pass routes valid.

What comes out
Inputs toward the Financial Reality Note.', '', null, 'Notion — Entrepalooza Curriculum & Evidence Lab · Module 6 working draft · Copy of Ashley Zeck workspace original · Oct 6, 2026 · edits here do not sync. Cross-links may still point to Ashley-workspace originals until rewritten.', '- Celebrate financially honest employment or pause as success.
- Stop invasive probing.
- Keep structural scarcity visible — not a character flaw.

- Not financial advice; refer out for crisis / debt / tax / benefits counseling.
- No spend / borrow / fundraise pressure.
- No invasive household disclosure.
- Do not treat employment-for-income as quitting entrepreneurship.
- Do not start a second Module 5 try inside Module 6.

- “Prove you’re financially ready.”
- “Money mindset is the real problem.”
- Investor-ready / ROI theater.
- Requiring Module 6 to finish Module 5.
- Funneling everyone back to “keep building the business.”', 'https://www.notion.so/3f1ca793c2c581e2a69bd80ffb9fde9f', 'Check What This Costs', 'Map what this try or next step actually cost', 'Existing card retained unchanged, as structure. Teaching on this card is not approved for participant delivery.', 'Money, time, labor, caregiving, support, affordability, and practical constraints.', 'pending_evaluator_and_clinical_review', '', '', 'Research and theory are used as design lenses, not as proof that Entrepalooza works. Related research does not prove that Entrepalooza works.', '', 8, 'Pass, respond in private, observe, pause, stop, or choose another direction.
